  "name": "aube-bump",
  "description": "Bump nub's vendored aube engine to a newer jdx/aube upstream. Invoke (via the Skill tool) whenever you need to pull upstream aube changes into `vendor/aube/**` — a new release, or arbitrary commits. Encodes the venue-less merge (build an ephemeral merge commit from nub's own objects with `git commit-tree`; no clone, no `nub-fork`, no push-back) and the two-conflict-list methodology: git's markers find TEXTUAL conflicts, the compiler finds SEMANTIC ones, both lists are machine-generated and exhaustive, so you never hand-review a diff. Also covers merge-base correctness (the single biggest lever), merge-not-rebase, `rerere`, the nub delta inventory that must survive, and the nub-side breaks upstream feature-gating causes. Supersedes the older `aube-sync` skill.",
  "stars": 4435,
